{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n9DoUdpUzhxrvAR7Wj","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `scripts/export_invoices.py` and committed it along with the `out/invoices.csv` it produced.\n\n**One difference from the customers export:** the customers export removes segment C customers. The commit that added that filter (`75776b2`) says those customers declined partner sharing, and that this applies to every record held on them, not just the customers table. So the invoices export also drops every invoice belonging to a segment C customer. Invoices have no segment column, so the script looks each one up in `tables/customers.csv` by `customer_id`.\n\n- **Result:** 8 of the 12 invoices were exported. The 4 left out all belong to customers 103 and 105, the only segment C customers, and I checked that the output contains none of their invoices.\n- **Commit message:** `export_invoices: add invoices export, excluding segment C`. This follows the `export_customers: …` style rather than starting with a month, because the commit doesn't touch `data/`. The month-first convention matters for data commits because the nightly import reads it to pick the month to load.\n- **January:** left as you asked. `data/2026-01.csv` is still untracked and wasn't included.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":366,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":21666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-71>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:34.800Z","request_id":"gen-1794703050-iMFlVA56znULPIFFZMSn"}
